gin:0.05pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;">Less: current portion of debt</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.29%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0.05pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:11pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.44%;border-bottom:1px solid #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0.05pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:8.89%;border-bottom:1px solid #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0.05pt 3.6pt 0.05pt 0pt;"> &#8212;</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.29%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0.05pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.44%;border-bottom:1px solid #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0.05pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:9.84%;border-bottom:1px solid #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0.05pt 3.6pt 0.05pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2020_o3-q8vMvZk2qb8-75R2X2Q" decimals="-3" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:LongTermDebtCurrent" scale="3" id="Tc_PQhzLux61U6nSpEt5ODHAw_8_6">3,609</ix:nonFraction></p></td></tr><tr><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:73.77%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0.05pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;">Debt, noncurrent portion</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.29%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0.05pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:11pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.44%;background:#cceeff;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0.05pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;">$</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:8.89%;background:#cceeff;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0.05pt 3.6pt 0.05pt 0pt;"> &#8212;</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.29%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0.05pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.44%;background:#cceeff;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0.05pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;">$</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:9.84%;background:#cceeff;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0.05pt 3.6pt 0.05pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2020_o3-q8vMvZk2qb8-75R2X2Q" decimals="-3" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:LongTermDebtNoncurrent" scale="3" id="Tc_rJM87EOUU0W0kTks2L-ntw_9_6">9,168</ix:nonFraction></p></td></tr></table></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;min-height:0.0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:0pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:12pt 0pt 12pt 18pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">CARES Act</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:14pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">On April 24, 2020, the Company entered into a PPP Loan agreement with Silicon Valley Bank (&#8220;SVB&#8221;) under the PPP, which is part of the CARES Act administered by the United States Small Business Administration (&#8220;SBA&#8221;). As part of the application for these funds, the Company in good faith, has certified that the current economic uncertainty made the loan request necessary to support the ongoing operations of the Company. This certification further requires the Company to take into account our current business activity and our ability to access other sources of liquidity sufficient to support ongoing operations in a manner that is not significantly detrimental to the business. Under this program, the Company received proceeds of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="Duration_4_24_2020_To_4_24_2020_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_rsls_PaycheckProtectionProgramLoanMember_VtpxykpA2EOvyAsIUb1p0g" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromIssuanceOfDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_5_SEs17BUkaSB5StV6VJjQ">1.0</ix:nonFraction> million from the PPP Loan. In accordance with the requirements of the PPP, the Company intends to use proceeds from the PPP Loan primarily for payroll costs, rent and utilities. The PPP Loan has a <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_aOeMbxxy7EmVx5GkCS33Hg" contextRef="As_Of_4_24_2020_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_rsls_PaycheckProtectionProgramLoanMember_emkX4-PL_Eqnvato6ABATA" decimals="4" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentInterestRateEffectivePercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_lIOrwtwV1Eyc-eZjOhBAig">1.00</ix:nonFraction>% interest rate per annum, matures on April 24, 2022 and is subject to the terms and conditions applicable to loans administered by the SBA under the PPP. Under the terms of PPP, all or certain amounts of the PPP Loan may be forgiven if they are used for qualifying expenses as described in the CARES Act. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:14pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">On February 23, 2021, the Company submitted the application for PPP loan forgiveness, in accordance with the terms and conditions of the SBA&#8217;s Loan Forgiveness Application (revised June 24, 2020). On March 1, 2021, the Company received confirmation from the SBA, the PPP Loan has been forgiven in full including all interest incurred. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:14pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">Under the provisions of the CARES Act, the Company is eligible for a refundable employee retention credit subject to certain criteria. The Company recognized a $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2021_To_12_31_2021_cWvT7aMRfkaBO8f1uL4WQA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="rsls:EmployeeRetentionCreditCaresAct" scale="6" id="Narr_9XeJpxH0zEunCnDXaAHtlg">0.5</ix:nonFraction> million employee recognition credit during the year ended December 31, 2021.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:14pt 0pt 12pt 18pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Credit Agreement</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:14pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">On March 25, 2020, the Company executed a credit agreement up to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_3_25_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_lCgRmLKtkEKZqzJMi2y4fA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_9nasX7IVp0azMT0BfSMw1Q">3.5</ix:nonFraction> million, with an investor (the &#8220;Lender&#8221;), who holds warrants in connection with the June 2019 and September 2019 private placement transactions. See Note 8 for additional details. On the day of closing, the Company received $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="Duration_3_25_2020_To_3_25_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_BLwmhOFFmEuLk3sTI_NVZw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromIssuanceOfDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_Wjh2nzpODUSUBBkrTVmh8A">2.5</ix:nonFraction> million and the additional $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_3_25_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_lCgRmLKtkEKZqzJMi2y4fA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="rsls:DebtInstrumentAdditionalBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_H7DaYSfmq0ymYqriTBr3IA">1.0</ix:nonFraction> million may be drawn from time to time <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_3_25_2020_To_3_25_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_BLwmhOFFmEuLk3sTI_NVZw" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="rsls:DebtInstrumentPeriodAfterClosingDateInWhichAdditionalAmountCanBeDrawn" id="Narr_bSP357y8mEmGM3z1QO3vqg">30 days</ix:nonNumeric> after the closing date but prior to <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_3_25_2020_To_3_25_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_BLwmhOFFmEuLk3sTI_NVZw" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="rsls:DebtInstrumentThresholdPeriodToDrawAdditionalAmount" id="Narr_2EUHbzDfWkmvwkUN4YQQsA">five months</ix:nonNumeric> after the closing date, in $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_3_25_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_lCgRmLKtkEKZqzJMi2y4fA" decimals="-3" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="rsls:DebtInstrumentMaximumAmountPerDraw" scale="3" id="Narr_jdoTQuP5NUKqUSsLC-m0oA">500</ix:nonFraction> thousand increments per draw. On June 23, 2020, the Company made the first additional draw of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="Duration_6_23_2020_To_6_23_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_Y_znr_nxo0K_lfB4An81xg" decimals="-3" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromIssuanceOfDebt" scale="3" id="Narr_SbLyo0u2XUimEbksN__K9w">500</ix:nonFraction> thousand and on July 29, 2020, the second $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="Duration_7_29_2020_To_7_29_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_23ltzN4eAEWnWyj1GJqJBQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromIssuanceOfDebt" scale="3" id="Narr_kw4jRyJmEEyisj7zbezAzg">500</ix:nonFraction> thousand draw was made. As required by the terms of this credit agreement, the lender exercised its warrants to purchase an aggregate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_UyDeH6EI8U2czXKPUA4y4g" contextRef="As_Of_4_15_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_Uj2YJt2p40iuIEi0Dkw-2A" decimals="INF" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:ClassOfWarrantOrRightNumberOfSecuritiesCalledByWarrantsOrRights" scale="0" id="Narr_iPNhBq95hkmbHLaJdn9zjw">101,717</ix:nonFraction> shares of common stock with a current exercise price of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_XsXECV5vEU2b4A8J3OA1qw" contextRef="As_Of_4_15_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_Uj2YJt2p40iuIEi0Dkw-2A" decimals="2" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:ClassOfWarrantOrRightExercisePriceOfWarrantsOrRights1" scale="0" id="Narr_Tt-3uu47s0WI0iHGv6YS8A">6.00</ix:nonFraction> per warrant on April 15, 2020, in which the Company received net proceeds of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="Duration_4_15_2020_To_4_15_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_AC9_TQ1aekybinuxbCNWhw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromWarrantExercises" scale="6" id="Narr_WBZPy_4KZEu-CAlgMnanKQ">0.6</ix:nonFraction> million. In addition, the Company issued to the lender <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_UyDeH6EI8U2czXKPUA4y4g" contextRef="Duration_3_25_2020_To_3_25_2020_us-gaap_ClassOfWarrantOrRightAxis_rsls_SeriesGWarrantsMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_ET00Ll73Vkq1HzUF5PPCVg" decimals="INF" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="rsls:WarrantsIssued" scale="0" id="Narr_titMdgcGbU67GxvsDBvMFA">24,000</ix:nonFraction> Series G warrants to purchase an aggregate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_UyDeH6EI8U2czXKPUA4y4g" contextRef="As_Of_3_25_2020_us-gaap_ClassOfWarrantOrRightAxis_rsls_SeriesGWarrantsMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_1oqV3_qwokiXNX8VK2MxXg" decimals="INF" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:ClassOfWarrantOrRightNumberOfSecuritiesCalledByWarrantsOrRights" scale="0" id="Narr_wnU0G9_2AUmRLDQVxL_rYg">24,000</ix:nonFraction> shares of common stock. As an inducement to the Lender to enter into the amendment and make the additional loans contemplated thereby, the Company issued to the Lender an additional <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_UyDeH6EI8U2czXKPUA4y4g" contextRef="Duration_9_14_2020_To_9_14_2020_us-gaap_ClassOfWarrantOrRightAxis_rsls_SeriesGWarrantsMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_xzNPj6K5PEO-dWzAuugCsg" decimals="INF" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="rsls:WarrantsIssued" scale="0" id="Narr_Zd_sqf3QUE-thn61ZiFVnw">24,000</ix:nonFraction> Series G warrants dated September 14, 2020, to purchase an aggregate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_UyDeH6EI8U2czXKPUA4y4g" contextRef="As_Of_9_14_2020_us-gaap_ClassOfWarrantOrRightAxis_rsls_SeriesGWarrantsMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_OZ9EZFF64EaeOx9_uP2cVw" decimals="INF" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:ClassOfWarrantOrRightNumberOfSecuritiesCalledByWarrantsOrRights" scale="0" id="Narr_5xdbH4jMd0Sz6O72ne1MZQ">24,000</ix:nonFraction> shares of common stock. The value of the original Series G warrants were recorded as part of the debt issuance costs. See Note 12 for additional details.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:14pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">On September 14, 2020, the Company and the Lender entered into an amendment to the credit agreement that increased the amount available under delayed draw term loans by $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_9_14_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementAmendmentMember_0-zTX3ftvUOnukbKzLUZiA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="rsls:DebtInstrumentAdditionalBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_DQ1RzSuG2UmjVss7D4iOVQ">2.0</ix:nonFraction> million. The Company borrowed $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="Duration_9_14_2020_To_9_14_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementAmendmentMember_4dHWT8Rbo0yxjUYXAUIc0A" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromIssuanceOfDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_dgDnw_hMw0qmml-twXE0vw">1.0</ix:nonFraction> million of the available amount immediately and the remaining $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_9_14_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementAmendmentMember_0-zTX3ftvUOnukbKzLUZiA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityRemainingBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_KL0DKsnQCU-u2zQw91vnJQ">1.0</ix:nonFraction> million will be available in increments of least $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_9_14_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementAmendmentMember_0-zTX3ftvUOnukbKzLUZiA" decimals="-3" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="rsls:DebtInstrumentMinimumAmountPerDraw" scale="3" id="Narr_Wnvz2OkjyUqFKZc4l_8seg">500</ix:nonFraction> thousand with at least <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_9_14_2020_To_9_14_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementAmendmentMember_4dHWT8Rbo0yxjUYXAUIc0A" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="rsls:MinimumNumberOfDaysBetweenBorrowings" id="Narr_M5-fMJRCRUepOtEFv0J6-Q">30 days</ix:nonNumeric> between </p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">F-41</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_gYytkH4_SEiyycDPV-Xf5g_cont1"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">borrowings and issued an additional <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_UyDeH6EI8U2czXKPUA4y4g" contextRef="Duration_9_14_2020_To_9_14_2020_us-gaap_ClassOfWarrantOrRightAxis_rsls_SeriesGWarrantsMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementAmendmentMember_3z7Fl6cf-UOiwdsK6R8zBg" decimals="INF" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="rsls:WarrantsIssued" scale="0" id="Narr_j82lVr-fsUm6r6VCdDLyrQ">24,000</ix:nonFraction> Series G Warrants. The Company evaluated the accounting related to the amendment and in conjunction with the warrants issued. Based on this analysis the Company determined the agreements are substantially different and extinguished the original credit agreement and recorded the amended credit agreement as a new debt at a fair value of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_9_14_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementAmendmentMember_0-zTX3ftvUOnukbKzLUZiA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:LongTermDebtFairValue" scale="6" id="Narr_46uo6mP2R0S-OTFtUkIGCg">3.9</ix:nonFraction> million. As a result in 2020, the Company recorded a debt discount of approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_9_14_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementAmendmentMember_0-zTX3ftvUOnukbKzLUZiA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentUnamortizedDiscount" scale="6" id="Narr_2VQMVrYGDEyrSh3enioKQA">0.6</ix:nonFraction> million and a $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="Duration_9_14_2020_To_9_14_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementAmendmentMember_4dHWT8Rbo0yxjUYXAUIc0A" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:GainsLossesOnExtinguishmentOfDebt" sign="-" scale="6" id="Narr_qjgk1EMr4Uqg_gN1v_sWFQ">2.4</ix:nonFraction> million loss on extinguishment of debt which is comprised of the fair value of the warrants and unamortized debt issuance cost with the original credit agreement, offset by the debt discount. Pursuant to the amendment of the credit agreement, the maturity date of the loans was March 31, 2021 and the loans bear interest at LIBOR plus <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_aOeMbxxy7EmVx5GkCS33Hg" contextRef="Duration_9_14_2020_To_9_14_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_us-gaap_VariableRateAxis_us-gaap_LondonInterbankOfferedRateLIBORMember_VR-82MpPVUOjC7JZeeHPrA" decimals="3" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentBasisSpreadOnVariableRate1" scale="-2" id="Narr_4_dse2D9lEGLSQxP7fTNKg">2.5</ix:nonFraction>%.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:14pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">On December 16, 2020, the Company and the Lender entered into the third amendment to the credit agreement that increased the amount available under delayed draw term loans by an additional $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="Duration_12_16_2020_To_12_16_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementFourthAmendmentMember_LvDTsEt46EiAyFOiCqqR6A" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromIssuanceOfDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_8NM7ylgCPEqGPCKqpJ2pQA">4.0</ix:nonFraction> million. The Company borrowed the entire $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_12_16_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementFourthAmendmentMember_tHbJZURg5kOjkcIymXojeQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="rsls:DebtInstrumentAdditionalBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_2r83Tn_aBUCfcTuIoEWxLg">4.0</ix:nonFraction> million of the available amount immediately and issued an additional <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_UyDeH6EI8U2czXKPUA4y4g" contextRef="Duration_12_16_2020_To_12_16_2020_us-gaap_ClassOfWarrantOrRightAxis_rsls_SeriesGWarrantsMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementFourthAmendmentMember_rWUO4_Cufkixd3tkU4LSxw" decimals="INF" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="rsls:WarrantsIssued" scale="0" id="Narr_Oj6SUUNc6kejwYKyb3duZQ">80,000</ix:nonFraction> Series G Warrants. The Company evaluated the accounting related to the amendment and in conjunction with the warrants issued. Based on this analysis the Company determined the agreements are substantially different and extinguished the original credit agreement and recorded the amended credit agreement as a new debt at a fair value of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_12_16_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementFourthAmendmentMember_tHbJZURg5kOjkcIymXojeQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:LongTermDebtFairValue" scale="6" id="Narr_sBgu7bHBaU2gI5RNX6VK6A">8.9</ix:nonFraction> million. As a result in 2020, the Company recorded a debt discount of approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_12_16_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementFourthAmendmentMember_tHbJZURg5kOjkcIymXojeQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentUnamortizedDiscount" scale="6" id="Narr_cJv3lrkAhEWRFyzuIoApDA">0.6</ix:nonFraction> million and a $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="Duration_12_16_2020_To_12_16_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementFourthAmendmentMember_LvDTsEt46EiAyFOiCqqR6A" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:GainsLossesOnExtinguishmentOfDebt" sign="-" scale="6" id="Narr_x-WhyJEChEOUNxqcV1-pJw">5.3</ix:nonFraction> million loss on extinguishment of debt which is comprised of the fair value of the warrants and unamortized debt discount cost with the original credit agreement, offset by the debt discount related to the new debt. At December 31, 2020 there was approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementFourthAmendmentMember__kXfh2sYe0iWV6cj9wRBuQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentUnamortizedDiscount" scale="6" id="Narr_rcPZmNsqlE6ix48Fv8pnUg">0.5</ix:nonFraction> million of unamortized debt discount. Pursuant to the amendment of the credit agreement, the maturity date of the loan was March 31, 2021 and the loans bear interest at LIBOR plus <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_aOeMbxxy7EmVx5GkCS33Hg" contextRef="Duration_12_16_2020_To_12_16_2020_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_us-gaap_VariableRateAxis_us-gaap_LondonInterbankOfferedRateLIBORMember_5Womh6TW10euvd5qt1ff8Q" decimals="3" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentBasisSpreadOnVariableRate1" scale="-2" id="Narr_VCaUXUT5bUShmiN49ic6Pw">2.5</ix:nonFraction>%.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:14pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">On January 19, 2021, the Company and the Lender entered into an amendment to the credit agreement that increased the amount available under delayed draw term loans by $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_1_19_2021_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_qJ-TgxTW6U2Dy6duRBJErw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="rsls:DebtInstrumentAdditionalBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_uIIVI0SPB0CtUOIRGVJyaA">1.0</ix:nonFraction> million, which was used to fund the $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_1_19_2021_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_qJ-TgxTW6U2Dy6duRBJErw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="rsls:ContractTerminationFeesPayable" scale="6" id="Narr_-nQwvCKr4keh0N-cWg5TPA">1.0</ix:nonFraction> million escrow fund securing the termination fee under the Merger Agreement and issued an additional <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_UyDeH6EI8U2czXKPUA4y4g" contextRef="As_Of_1_19_2021_us-gaap_ClassOfWarrantOrRightAxis_rsls_SeriesGWarrantsMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_CkWcaP6oyECWqBRx2VOkKg" decimals="INF" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:ClassOfWarrantOrRightNumberOfSecuritiesCalledByWarrantsOrRights" scale="0" id="Narr_yVf97WK0-UiXi5lXwTgf2Q">20,000</ix:nonFraction> Series G Warrants. The Company evaluated the accounting related to the amendment and in conjunction with the warrants issued. Based on this analysis the Company determined the agreements are substantially different and extinguished the original credit agreement and recorded the amended credit agreement as a new debt at a fair value of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_1_19_2021_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_qJ-TgxTW6U2Dy6duRBJErw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:LongTermDebtFairValue" scale="6" id="Narr_ZExR65kvmUWtoADuftHtZw">10.0</ix:nonFraction> million. As a result, the Company recorded a debt discount of approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_1_19_2021_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_qJ-TgxTW6U2Dy6duRBJErw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentUnamortizedDiscount" scale="6" id="Narr_JE7Vew0-h0inqSLTvIF7Tg">0.5</ix:nonFraction> million and a $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="Duration_1_19_2021_To_1_19_2021_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_4bgMIvCjZkCJCU952xeohA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:GainsLossesOnExtinguishmentOfDebt" sign="-" scale="6" id="Narr_PuM2sols5ES_btsue34oIg">3.0</ix:nonFraction> million loss on extinguishment of debt, which is comprised of the fair value of the warrants and unamortized debt issuance cost with the original credit agreement, offset by the debt discount. Pursuant to the amendment of the credit agreement, the maturity date of the loans are March 31, 2021 and the loans bear interest at LIBOR plus <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_aOeMbxxy7EmVx5GkCS33Hg" contextRef="Duration_1_19_2021_To_1_19_2021_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_us-gaap_VariableRateAxis_us-gaap_LondonInterbankOfferedRateLIBORMember_bJzs71R0vEq6Q3RQjWdJcQ" decimals="3" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentBasisSpreadOnVariableRate1" scale="-2" id="Narr_WwS6LE1nqEaDtZCkoMdYHQ">2.5</ix:nonFraction>%.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:14pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">On March 10, 2021, the Company and the Lender entered into an amendment to the credit agreement that extended the maturity date from March 31, 2021 to March 31, 2022. The Company has accounted for this amendment as a debt modification. The associated unamortized debt discount on the January 19, 2021 amendment of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="Duration_1_19_2021_To_1_19_2021_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_4bgMIvCjZkCJCU952xeohA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:InterestExpenseDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_1GkWgUUWYUOYaWth79a9Dg">0.1</ix:nonFraction> million will be amortized as interest expense over the term of the amended credit agreement.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:14pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">On June 28, 2021, the Company entered into a warrant exercise agreement with existing investors, including the Lender, to exercise certain outstanding warrants. For further details on this transaction see Note 9. The Company used some of the proceeds from this transaction to pay off the $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="Duration_6_28_2021_To_6_28_2021_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementMember_LZZnLNaCKkmJi0NPUPvJmQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:RepaymentsOfLongTermDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_IPHoNNyEPEyCqYiZpNmGPw">10.5</ix:nonFraction> million of debt outstanding under the credit agreement. At December 31, 2021, there was <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2021_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_rsls_CreditAgreementFourthAmendmentMember_7kUjOPRnGkiGCKYJykpWHA" decimals="-5" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:LongTermDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_DU1WNCw6REeAiujJacjxxA">no</ix:nonFraction> outstanding amount under the credit agreement.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:14pt 0pt 0pt 18pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Asset Purchase Consideration Payable</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:14pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">The asset purchase consideration payable related to the Company&#8217;s December 2018 acquisition of the Lap-Band product line from Apollo Endosurgery, Inc. (&#8220;Apollo&#8221;), was initially recorded at net present value using a discount rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2021_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SecuredDebtMember_us-gaap_MeasurementInputTypeAxis_us-gaap_MeasurementInputDiscountRateMember_C5gNMzNky0CioxsyZEaAxg" decimals="3" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentMeasurementInput" scale="-2" id="Narr_xtQa25cTpkiPpYBLM2Gv9Q">5.1</ix:nonFraction>%. The asset purchase consideration payable was originally secured by a first security interest in substantially all of the Company&#8217;s assets, but that security interest terminated in accordance with its terms in October 2019. At December 31, 2021, the Company had paid off the purchase consideration in full.</p></ix:continuation><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2021_To_12_31_2021_cWvT7aMRfkaBO8f1uL4WQA" name="us-gaap:LesseeOperatingLeasesTextBlock" id="Tb_HorxF0dtUUuxTMzQv3zTJQ" continuedAt="Tb_HorxF0dtUUuxTMzQv3zTJQ_cont1" escape="true"><table style="border-collapse:collapse;border:0;"><tr><td style="vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:14pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">(9)</b></p></td><td style="padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:14pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Leases</b></p></td></tr></table><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Company had noncancelable operating leases for office and warehouse space in San Clemente and Carlsbad, California, as well as and noncancelable operating leases for certain office equipment that expire at various dates through 2022. The Company does not have any short-term leases or financing lease arrangements and the effects of any lease modifications have not been material. Certain of the Company&#8217;s equipment leases include variable lease payments that are adjusted periodically based on actual usage. Lease and non-lease components are accounted for separately. </p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">F-42</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><a id="Tc_8_av-3at3kGJAol9msLtSQ_1_0"></a><a id="Tc_BuSSZ8pKZ0asRksw30evtQ_2_0"></a><a id="Tc_9DhStedXfkCv8u_x71wHcg_2_2"></a><a id="Tc_-858DOGQhUqjL_FCZpBOkg_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_4Vhsqm748kSOTEagxGUibQ_4_2"></a><a id="Tc_ymfcUOAmt0mgfADDbKqXAg_5_0"></a><a id="Tc_gbm1CIrTIUmGMXYTKgC5sA_5_3"></a><a id="Tc_Ld7FFBs4n0i61996yEvEog_6_0"></a><a id="Tc_g800aR9tiE-yM25SyqVFIQ_6_2"></a><a id="Tc_PzjTZcogvk-IbhblD-u6xA_8_0"></a><a id="Tc_tsP-jI0itkeepiKUp-fudw_9_0"></a><a id="Tc_rcxU06-lbkS03BsrAd_Y8A_9_2"></a><a id="Tc_dU2o0HbbZ0iOnIeUs65_fQ_1_0"></a><a id="Tc_MzYxdVxm20iaOpwAr5Vj1w_2_0"></a><a id="Tc_iVMaH1M-bUm_o74XjR-sCg_2_2"></a><a id="Tc_R_JpSUp1rEuHL5jLHgF1rg_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_SZytZiNjM0GdztgqkIUlwQ_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_nHru1V9QQkOP-P_KS6R6qQ_5_0"></a><a id="Tc_LsDVgJyhMUue2EJk9uuM7g_5_2"></a><a id="Tc_Jeu8NMVlQkenaFi9PZuCvg_7_0"></a><a id="Tc_iKhVdCR-ZEW5ALc46WIYxA_8_0"></a><ix:continuation id="Tb_HorxF0dtUUuxTMzQv3zTJQ_cont1"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Company determines the lease term as the noncancelable period of the lease, and may include options to extend or terminated the lease when reasonably certain that the Company will exercise that option. Leases with a term of 12 months or less are not recognized on the balance sheet. The Company uses its incremental borrowing rate based on the information available at lease commencement in determining the present value of unpaid lease payments. Right-of-use assets also include any lease payments made at or before lease commencement and any initial direct costs incurred, and exclude any lease incentives received.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:14pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Operating lease costs for the years ended December 31, 2021 and 2020, were $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2021_To_12_31_2021_cWvT7aMRfkaBO8f1uL4WQA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:OperatingLeaseCost" scale="6" id="Narr_VSbCPr6L7kKzZKQlTQVH_w">0.6</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_95AsBmQhZ0-8JYazjfgbjg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2020_To_12_31_2020_BwNwdEJ460GPPlLl1A9Hbg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:OperatingLeaseCost" scale="6" id="Narr_R8g1gHgAmEGf-oId1v2bxA">0.3</ix:nonFraction> million, respectively. Variable lease costs were not material.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Supplemental information related to operating leases is as follows:</p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2021_To_12_31_2021_cWvT7aMRfkaBO8f1uL4WQA" name="rsls:ScheduleOfAssetsAndLiabilitiesAndCashFlowLesseeOperatingLeaseTableTextBlock" id="Tb_9ZMDcZ76p0G2nl99OPc0Rg" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;min-height:0.0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:0pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16pt;height:max-content;padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;width:100%;"><tr style="height:1pt;"><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:85.1%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-siz